Today, significant progress was made in finalizing the code for both competition challenges. The team focused on optimizing the navigation algorithms and enhancing the integration of sensor data from the VL53L1X Time-of-Flight sensors and the RPLidar A1. Multiple test runs were conducted to ensure the system operates reliably under competition conditions, with adjustments made to improve obstacle detection accuracy and path planning efficiency. The codebase was refined for stability, and all components are now functioning as expected. Final checks and performance evaluations will continue to ensure readiness for the competition.

